        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Consider a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=2$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 2+\\text{nullity}(A) & =2 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
